significant concern among the group. Compared with the other candidates, whose cooperation or communication deficits are equally or more pronounced, B appears to have the best balance of strengths for a long\u2011distance pilot, provided we address the teamwork behavior through targeted training and monitoring.\n**Provisional vote:** Candidate\u202fB, with the recommendation to include a focused crew\u2011resource\u2011management development plan.", "thoughts": "We have just asked Agent 1 and got answer confirming concern about B's crew cooperation. Now we need to produce public message: share this evidence, maybe compare B with others on crew cooperation, and give provisional recommendation. We have other candidate info: A is unfriendly, D is loner, C difficulty communicating, egocentric. So crew cooperation concerns across candidates. Need to identify strongest candidate overall.\n\nWe have evidence:\n\nA: unfriendly, eats unhealthily (maybe reliability?), good leadership, anticipates danger, sees complex connections, spatial vision. But unfriendly may affect crew cooperation.\n\nB: conscientious, handles stress well, good weather assessment, excellent computer skills, but pretentious, wrong tone, uncooperative, grumpy.\n\nC: quick correct decisions, difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, loner.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's map:\n\nA: leadership, anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision => technical competence, decision quality, attention. Unfriendly => crew cooperation, professional communication maybe poor. Eating unhealthily maybe reliability? Not sure.\n\nB: conscientious => reliability, handles stress well => stress resilience, good weather assessment => technical competence, computer skills => technical, but pretentious, wrong tone, uncooperative => crew cooperation, professional communication concerns.\n\nC: quick correct decisions => decision quality, excellent attention => attention, puts concern for others => maybe crew cooperation positive, but difficulty communicating, egocentric => communication issues, not willing to further education => adaptability/feedback orientation low.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately => stress resilience, concentrates well => attention, solves problems extremely well => technical competence, takes responsibility seriously => responsibility, moody, loner => crew cooperation, professional communication concerns.\n\nWe need to decide best overall. Which candidate has strongest overall with minimal concerns? B has strong reliability and stress, but crew cooperation concerns. C has good decision and attention, but communication and adaptability issues. D has strong technical, responsibility, but moody/loner. A has strong technical, but unfriendly.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B: strong reliability, stress, technical, but crew cooperation concerns may be mitigated? B's uncooperative and grumpy could be serious for cockpit. C's egocentric and communication issues also serious. D's moody/loner also serious. A's unfriendly also serious. All have some concerns. Need to weigh.\n\nMaybe B's strengths outweigh concerns? He is conscientious, handles stress, good technical. Crew cooperation is a concern but could be trained. C's communication difficulty and unwillingness to further education may be more limiting. D's moody/loner may affect crew. A's unfriendly may affect crew.\n\nThus provisional recommendation: Candidate B, but note crew cooperation concern.\n\nNow produce public message: share evidence about B's crew cooperation, compare with others, state provisional vote."}
